WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.790
You can touch a keyboard.
You cannot touch a game.

2
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.979
One is hardware. One is software.
Together they make a computer work.

3
00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:18.402
Hardware is the parts you can touch.
A screen, a keyboard, a speaker.

4
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:24.102
Software is the programs that run on them.
A game to play, a drawing app to draw with.

5
00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:27.573
You can pick up a keyboard.
You cannot pick up a game.

6
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:31.879
Is the drawing app the same thing
as the tablet? No, it is not.

7
00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:35.861
The tablet is hardware. The
apps are software running on it.

8
00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:41.423
Every part of a laptop has a job.
That job is called its function.

9
00:00:41.643 --> 00:00:46.287
The screen shows pictures and
words. The keyboard puts letters in.

10
00:00:46.507 --> 00:00:50.315
The touchpad moves the pointer.
The camera takes pictures.

11
00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:54.807
The speaker makes sound. The charger
plugs into the charging port.

12
00:00:55.027 --> 00:00:59.532
Six parts, and six jobs. Name
a part, then say its function.

13
00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:03.422
A tablet is made to be easy
to use. Look at its parts.

14
00:01:03.642 --> 00:01:07.775
The touchscreen is the keyboard,
the mouse and the screen in one.

15
00:01:07.995 --> 00:01:10.921
The home button always
takes you back to the start.

16
00:01:11.141 --> 00:01:14.810
The volume buttons stick out, so
you can find them without looking.

17
00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.211
A device is user-friendly when you
can use it without being taught.

18
00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:23.099
An icon is the little picture
you press to open a program.

19
00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:27.824
An envelope for mail. A camera
for photos. No reading needed.

20
00:01:28.044 --> 00:01:31.992
Big buttons you can hit with a
finger. A screen you point at.

21
00:01:32.212 --> 00:01:35.787
Or a voice you can talk to.
Designers work hard on this.

22
00:01:36.287 --> 00:01:40.513
Information goes into a computer,
and information comes out again.

23
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:46.585
An input device sends information in.
A keyboard, a mouse, a microphone.

24
00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:51.960
An output device sends it out.
A screen, a speaker, a printer.

25
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.452
Input does not mean plugged in.
It means information going in.

26
00:01:56.672 --> 00:02:00.666
You press jump on the controller.
The printer prints your drawing.

27
00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:04.881
Not every input device has
keys. Some of them just look.

28
00:02:05.101 --> 00:02:08.352
A barcode reader looks at
the stripes on a packet.

29
00:02:08.572 --> 00:02:13.309
It puts the number straight into the
till. That is faster than typing.

30
00:02:13.529 --> 00:02:17.755
And it never mistypes. A
microphone puts your voice in.

31
00:02:17.975 --> 00:02:22.247
A camera puts a picture in.
All of them are input devices.

32
00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:26.648
Hardware is the parts you can
touch. Software is the programs.

33
00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:30.212
Every part has a function,
which is the job it does.

34
00:02:30.432 --> 00:02:34.937
Input devices send information
in. Output devices send it out.

35
00:02:35.157 --> 00:02:38.500
And a user-friendly device
is one that anybody can use.
